@apiDocument(#{`openapi`:"3.0.3",`info`:#{`title`:"IYA STS reports",`version`:"1",`description`:"The reports API. Every operation takes an access token for this realm's /report-api carrying report:use or report:admin — the public client sts-report's, DPoP-bound and sent as Authorization: DPoP, or an application's own (client_credentials) where the application is a member of REPORT_USE or REPORT_ADMIN and declares the scope. The scopes are the permissions of those two roles; the access-control policy decides every definition and job: an owner their own, a report administrator every one, a shared group's member reading and running one shared with them, an application only what it defined. A job id is not an authorization: retrieving a result takes the same token. Paths are after the realm prefix; the default realm has none. The catalog is the field reference. A query names one source. An offset, a second source and a SQL statement are invalid_query. Errors are English. The body never carries an STS-REPORT code."},`components`:#{`securitySchemes`:#{`dpop`:#{`type`:"http",`scheme`:"bearer",`bearerFormat`:"JWT",`description`:"Send the access token as Authorization: DPoP, with a DPoP proof. Bearer is refused for this token."}}},`x-iya-doc`:"report"})
